    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d366">

                <pb facs="0529" n="433" sameAs="frus:frus1921v02/pg433"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">812.00/25033: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Minister in Cuba</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Long</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1921-06-11T14:00:00-04:00"><hi rendition="#italic">June 11, 1921—2
                                p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>117. For General Crowder.</p>
                <p>Your 70, June 10, 10 a.m.</p>
                <p>Advise the President confidentially that this Government will greatly appreciate
                    it if recognition by Cuba of the present Government of Mexico should be made
                    coincident with recognition by the United States.</p>
                <p>A copy of the statement issued to the press by this Department on June 7,<anchor
                        n="50" xml:id="d366-f1"/> regarding the relations between the United States
                    and Mexico, will be transmitted to you by the next mail for your information and
                    for that of Dr. Zayas.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hughes</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d366-f1" n="50" xml:id="d366-f1-content">
                <p>Quoted in telegram no. 85, June 8, 1921, to the Chargé in Mexico, <ref
                        target="#pg406">p. 406</ref>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
